{"id": "lg_elec-2026-10-07-006", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 1.0, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "涉及財報", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "Spotlight on LG Display - the WOLED pioneer, Apple's second OLED supplier, and its new bet on maskless OLED production", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display\">LG Display</a> (LGD) is the world's second-largest OLED producer by revenue, and the company that turned OLED TVs from a prototype into an industry. It is also the only display maker with volume positions at both ends of the OLED market: large-area WOLED panels for TVs and monitors, and small and medium flexible AMOLEDs for smartphones, watches, tablets and cars.</p><img class=\"align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/2026", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/spotlight-lg-display-woled-pioneer-apples-second-oled-supplier-and-its-new-bet", "type": "rss"}]}
